-- title:
--   Bounded rigidification exponent on a fixed edge chart
-- statement:
--   The setting is that of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison at a fixed prime.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Two primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a level $N \neq 0$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Coefficient rings.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal{O}$ for the ideal $(\pi)$, residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal{O}$. Next, a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal{O}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, subject to: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, maximality of that ideal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`). A monoid homomorphism $vdet : GL_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is given, characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data and moduli.** Rationals $a, b$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$, and a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}$ with a point assignment `pt` on fake elliptic curves of level $N$ which is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$, prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a fine moduli space $M$ for curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and a group $G$ acting by automorphisms of $M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ forming a level twist action (`hρ`). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base, invariant under $G$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`) together with two degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1$ to $\mathcal{X}$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1$ given on points by level-$\ell$ isogenies (`hd₀`, `hd₁`). Two endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over the base, described on points by the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, an idele $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is Eichler of level $Nr$, an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, and the height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma t$ of the unit group, equal to [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37) (`hΓt`). Families $s$, $sf$ indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ subject to `hs` (four clauses): the component of $sf_\ell$ at a prime not containing $r$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$, its component at a prime containing $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and the groups $\Gamma t_\ell = \Gamma t \cap s_\ell \Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Coordinates on the order.** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is an order coordinate system $\Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, semilinear multiplicativity involving the Witt Frobenius, injective, dense, and computing reduced traces).
--
--   **Special fibre and the endomorphism dictionary.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ over the same ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and the assertion that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). Families $e, e' : \Gamma t \to \mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and exponents $\mathrm{deg} : \Gamma t \to \mathbb{N}$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` and `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) say: each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\mathrm{deg}\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; the assignment is multiplicative and takes rational integral scalars to multiplications, both up to powers of $r$, and only scalar $\gamma$ give multiplications; for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ has an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser inducing $e\gamma$ on formal coordinates with image $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; the action of $\Gamma t$ on the level-$n$ structure is labelled by elements of $\Lambda$ multiplicatively modulo $n$; every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level structure on a fake elliptic curve pulled back from $A_0$ over an algebraically closed field comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and, for an order $R_2 \le R_1$ all of whose $R_1$-multiples become integral after multiplication by a power of $r$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`), a second family $\hat e : R_2 \to \mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base which is additive on points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action, preserves the level, is unital and multiplicative, takes integers to multiplications, satisfies $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, agrees with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma t$, and admits a matrix normalisation simultaneously for $\Gamma t$ and for $R_2$ with one conjugator $g$.
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a comparison $\eta$ sending rigidified modules over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent to points of $MD$, subject to `hη` (three clauses): on Noetherian bases, $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidified modules precisely up to isomorphism; $\eta$ is natural for ring maps compatible with the structure morphisms on admissible objects; and every point of $MD$ over a Noetherian base becomes $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified module after localising at the members of a finite family generating the unit ideal. Further, an injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image has bounded denominators in both directions (`hE₀`).
--
--   **The period map $eD$.** For each Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $eD$ from the $\mathcal{O}$-points of $MD$ to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $Onr \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, subject to: naturality in $B$ (`hnatD`), bijectivity (`hbijD`), the first component being the structure map $\psi$ of the point (`hfstD`), the translation law turning the action of $g \in GL_2(K_0)$ on $MD$-points into the twisted action on pairs, in which the algebra map is twisted by $Fr^{-vdet(g)}$ and the datum is pulled back along $g^{-1}$ (`hGLD`), the $\pi$-translation law, which replaces the algebra map by its single Frobenius twist and leaves the datum unchanged (`hPiD`), and existence of $\pi$-translates (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Bounded exponent on edge charts.** The hypothesis `hbdd` states that for all full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices $M' \subseteq M$ in $K_0^2$ with $\pi M \subseteq M'$ there is $N_\gamma \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for every Noetherian local Artinian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with algebraically closed residue field in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and every point $y$ of $MD$ over $B$ whose Deligne datum $(eD\,y)_2$ lies in the edge chart attached to $(M', M)$, the point $y$ is $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified module $t$ with $t.n \le N_\gamma$.
--
--   **Transport data.** A ring map $\kappa$ from $Onr/\pi$ to $Onr/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`); an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny $\Phi \to X_0 \circ \kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`); a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. On the special fibre, an Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$: a curve $A_{0w}$ with maps $aw$, $aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), and $bw$, $bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), such that $aw \circ bw$ is matched with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ in the same matrix normalisation as the elements of $\Gamma t$ (`hJOINTw`).
--
--   **The rigidification transport $\Xi$.** For each Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$, a map $\Xi$ from rigidified curves over $B$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$ to $MD$-points over $B$, subject to: over connected $B$ the structure map of $\Xi(x)$ is a Frobenius twist $Fr^{k}\psi$ (`hΞleg`); naturality under pullback of rigidified curves (`hΞnat`); invariance under isomorphisms of the underlying curves which match the rigidifications up to powers of $r$ (`hΞiso`); and the explicit description `hΞdef`: over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, for a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve via `coord` there are $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified module $t$ with $t.X = X$, related to the rigidification by `IsRigTransport θ₀ κ β₀` with shift $j$, admissible for the $(-j)$-twist of $\psi$, such that $\Xi(x)$ is the point with structure map $Fr^{-j}\psi$ and underlying class $\eta\,t$.
--
--   **Normalisation and the two equivariance laws.** An element $g_0 \in GL_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and: `heqΓ` states that if two rigidifications of the same curve over a connected base differ by translation by $e\gamma$, then the corresponding $MD$-points are related by the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb{Z}$; `heqW` states the analogous law for the Atkin–Lehner step at $\bar r$ on a base in which $\bar r$ is invertible, with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ in place of $\iota_0(\gamma)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every pair of full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices $M'$, $M$ in $K_0^2$ with $M' \subseteq M$ and $\pi M \subseteq M'$ there exists $d_\gamma \in \mathbb{N}$ with the following property. Let $S$ be a Noetherian local Artinian ring with algebraically closed residue field, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, let $\psi_S : Onr \to S$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, and let $x$ be a rigidified curve over $S$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi_S$, that is, a fake elliptic curve $x.1$ of level $N$ over $S$ together with a rigidification $x.2$. Suppose that the Deligne datum obtained from the second component of $eD\,S\,hS\,(\Xi\,S\,\psi_S\,hS\,x)$ by `DeligneDatum.pullback π S (g₀⁻¹)⁻¹` lies in the edge chart attached to $(M', M)$, that is, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $S$ the conditions `EdgeNondegAt` hold: $M' \subseteq M$, $\pi M \subseteq M'$, no $v \in M \setminus M'$ has $1 \otimes v$ in the sum of the line at $M$ with $\mathfrak{p}$ times the whole base change, and no $v' \in M'$ outside $\pi M$ has $1 \otimes v'$ in the sum of the line at $M'$ with $\mathfrak{p}$ times the whole base change. Then there exists a rigidification $\rho'$ of the same curve $x.1$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi_S$ such that
--
--   1. $\rho'.d \le d_\gamma$, i.e. the degree exponent of the isogeny pair contained in $\rho'$ is bounded by $d_\gamma$; and
--
--   2. $x.2$ and $\rho'$ are equivalent in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.Equiv hΛℤ`: there are morphisms $u$ between the reductions of the curve components and $u_A$ between the reductions of the $A_0$-components satisfying `IsComparison`, and natural numbers $i, j$ with $u$ followed by $\rho'.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{i}$ equal to $x.2.\varphi$ followed by $u_A$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j}$.
--
--   The bound $d_\gamma$ depends only on the pair of lattices $(M', M)$, and in particular is uniform in $S$, in $\psi_S$ and in $x$.
--
--   This is the effectivity input of the fine-level Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: on a single edge chart of the Drinfeld upper half plane, the exponent of the $r$-power isogeny occurring in a rigidification can be normalised within its equivalence class by a bound depending only on the chart. It converts the bounded-exponent statement `hbdd` for the period map $eD$ into a bound on the rigidification side, and is used in the per-chart representability and open-immersion statements for the fixed-exponent strata windows.
